  Part 2 — The 4 User-Identified Gaps (Now Verified)

  GAP 1 ✗ — Global Approvals Queue (Inbox)

  Verified state: Approval actions exist per-module (POST /journal-entries/{id}/approve, /invoices/{id}/approve,
  /payments/{id}/approve, /source-documents/{id}/approve). There is zero aggregation — no repository query, no service
  method, no controller that collects PENDING_APPROVAL items across modules.

  Frontend impact: Dashboard.vue approval queue card and the full Approvals.vue view both need a single endpoint returning
  pending items from all modules, typed so the UI can route the approve/reject action back to the right module endpoint.

  What needs building:
  GET /api/v1/approvals
    ?type=JOURNAL|INVOICE|PAYMENT|SOURCE_DOC   (optional filter)
    &assignedTo=me                              (optional — only items I can approve)

  Response: {
    total: 12,
    items: [
      { id, type: "JOURNAL_ENTRY", ref, title, amount, currency,
        submittedBy, submittedAt, status: "PENDING_APPROVAL",
        approveUrl: "/api/v1/journal-entries/{id}/approve",
        rejectUrl:  "/api/v1/journal-entries/{id}/reject" }
    ]
  }

  Implementation approach: a new GlobalApprovalController with an ApprovalAggregatorService that runs 4 repository queries
  (journals, invoices, payments, source docs) filtered by status = PENDING_APPROVAL and entityId = caller's org, then merges
   and sorts by submittedAt desc.

