  Part 4 — Demo Mode / Production Mode Architecture

  This is a critical cross-cutting concern that must be designed before any integration begins. Every fetch() call in the
  frontend must be mode-aware.

  Design: useAppMode composable + Organization setting

  How it works:
  - The Organization profile page has a Demo / Production toggle
  - The selected mode is persisted in localStorage (survives refresh, scoped per browser)
  - A central composable useAppMode() exposes the current mode
  - Every data-fetching call goes through a single API layer (src/api/) that the composable governs — in Demo mode it
  returns static data from data/index.js, in Production mode it calls the real backend

  src/
  ├── composables/
  │   └── useAppMode.js          ← single source of truth for mode
  ├── api/
  │   ├── index.js               ← barrel: re-exports all resource APIs
  │   ├── journals.js            ← getJournals(), createJournal(), etc.
  │   ├── invoices.js
  │   ├── dashboard.js
  │   ├── approvals.js
  │   └── ...                    ← one file per resource
  └── data/
      └── index.js               ← untouched demo data (current file)

  useAppMode.js:
  import { ref, readonly } from 'vue'

  const DEMO = 'demo'
  const PROD = 'production'
  const _mode = ref(localStorage.getItem('qsuite_mode') || DEMO)

  export function useAppMode() {
    function setMode(m) {
      _mode.value = m
      localStorage.setItem('qsuite_mode', m)
    }
    return {
      mode: readonly(_mode),
      isDemo: computed(() => _mode.value === DEMO),
      isProd: computed(() => _mode.value === PROD),
      setMode,
    }
  }

  Example API module (src/api/journals.js):
  import { useAppMode } from '@/composables/useAppMode'
  import { JOURNALS } from '@/data/index.js'

  const BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL

  export async function getJournals(params = {}) {
    const { isDemo } = useAppMode()
    if (isDemo.value) return { data: JOURNALS, total: JOURNALS.length }
    const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/journal-entries?${new URLSearchParams(params)}`, {
      headers: authHeaders()
    })
    return res.json()
  }

  export async function approveJournal(id) {
    const { isDemo } = useAppMode()
    if (isDemo.value) return { success: true }   // no-op in demo
    const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/journal-entries/${id}/approve`, {
      method: 'POST', headers: authHeaders()
    })
    return res.json()
  }

